# Vendored dependencies (D052).
#
# Pinned by version and verified by SHA-256. `tools/vendor.sh <name>` fetches and
# installs one; `tools/vendor.sh --verify` checks that no installed tree has
# drifted from its pin. Trees are committed to git, so a build needs no network.
#
# Adding a dependency requires a decision entry in docs/01-decisions.md. The list
# is meant to stay at four (D035).
#
# columns: name  version  sha256  url  archive-member

sqlite   3.53.0400  1e71ddf93849c6a6ecf58b827c0692073d2dd7ee40196158068f7b29f422e87d  https://www.sqlite.org/2026/sqlite-amalgamation-3530400.zip  sqlite-amalgamation-3530400
mbedtls  3.6.7      a7e8bcbec0e6f761b4af24f25677626b35f762f68eef79c08677a363212d11f6  https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls/releases/download/mbedtls-3.6.7/mbedtls-3.6.7.tar.bz2  mbedtls-3.6.7

# Notes on the pins:
#
# sqlite   The amalgamation, not the full source tree: one .c and one .h, which is
#          the form the compile-time SQL checker (D033) links against.
#
# mbedtls  The 3.6 LTS branch, deliberately, not 4.x. 4.x moved to a PSA-only
#          crypto API split across a second repository; 3.6 is long-term support
#          with security fixes, a stable API, and a single tree. That is the
#          conservative choice for a project promising one minor release a year
#          (D035). The recorded checksum matches upstream's published
#          mbedtls-3.6.7-sha256sum.txt.
#
# Not yet pinned, and pinned when the version that needs them is built:
#   libdeflate  gzip, v0.3
#   argon2      password hashing, v0.4
